  "commemorated_topic": "Archeological complex of Tunanmarca",
  "comments": "These ruins date back to the Wanka civilization, which predated the Incas and occupied the Mantaro valley.<br />\r\nThis city comprised some 4,300 chullpas, small circular buildings organized in groups around central courtyards and protected by walls. It was divided into two districts separated by a central avenue, and boasted a complex hydraulic system capable of providing drinking water for the entire population, estimated at 20,000. It was populated between the thirteenth and sixteenth centuries AD.",
